  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/27-puffers/chelonodon-patoca-2/",
      "html": "<p>Brackish water puffer. Adults reach up to 30 cm. Best kept in brackish water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/27-puffers/chelonodon-patoca-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species Chelonodon patoca has a wide distribution in the Indian Ocean. It is often placed in the genus Chelonodontops in recent times. This stock was received from Thailand.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/27-puffers/chelonodon-patoca-2/",
      "html": "<p>Adult specimens usually live in the sea, while young fish live in brackish water and occasionally swim far upstream.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/27-puffers/chelonodon-patoca-2/",
      "html": "<p>One should have a sandy bottom in the aquarium, as C. patoca likes to bury itself from time to time.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/27-puffers/chelonodon-patoca-2/",
      "html": "<p>Sadly, many individuals of this beautiful fish become fin biters. So one should keep them only along with fast fish that can avoid the attacks of the puffer. Otherwise C. patoca is easy to keep and, like most pufferfishes, very interesting.</p>"
    }
  ],
